welcome back to the david pakman show i  am faring cousins from ring of fire  sitting in for david pakman today and  don't forget you can find me on youtube  youtube.com slash the ring of fire  and youtube.com slash fahren balanced  we had a lot of movement over this past  weekend  on the infrastructure bill the slim down  infrastructure bill we still of course  have reconciliation on the other part  which  unfortunately not going so well but  let's talk about what is kind of  going well at this point senate did  vote to move forward on infrastructure  negotiations  infrastructure debate really good like i  said  positive developments it looks like you  are getting some republicans  who are starting to come around to this  obviously whatever happens in the senate  this thing  still has to go through the house of  representatives  where it's going to go through even more  changes so far from over at this point  but we are seeing forward  progress but there's somebody who's not  happy about forward progress somebody  who has been shouting for two weeks now  that forward progress is a bad thing and  you guessed it ladies and gentlemen that  person is none other  than former president donald j  trump trump issued a warning  to republicans over the weekend he said  joe biden's infrastructure bill is a  disgrace  will be very hard for me to endorse  anyone foolish enough to vote in favor  of this deal  you know what i love about that  statement it's such a small statement  okay  it's so tiny it's just a little sentence  two sentences i guess technically  but uh it says so much  about american politics today not just  about trump not just about the  republican party but it says so much  about politics  so i have to break this statement down  again this tiny little statement i'm  breaking it down  three different ways the first one  is take off partisan blinders get rid of  hatred for trump  get rid of support for infrastructure  all of that let's just look at this  as political strategy because what i'm  going to say here might shock you  from a strategy standpoint  trump is right i know i know uh  it's weird to even say it but  he's right what's the republicans best  chance to win in the 2022 midterms  showing the public that the democrats  couldn't get anything done  showing the public that all these lofty  goals of the democratic party  fell flat and of course by doing that  they're going to omit the part where  they're the ones who made it all fail  that's how the talking point works  but mitch mcconnell was very clear a  couple months ago when he said on camera  we've got to make sure that they can't  move forward on their agenda because  mcconnell knows the same thing  they've got to make a pitch to voters  because so far all their attacks on  biden  have failed that's another important  thing to remember folks  all their attacks have failed so far  because they don't have anything real  to attack him on so if they give him  this infrastructure package that is a  big win for the democratic party  not as big as it should have been  certainly not as big as they were asking  for in the plan  but if the democrats produce if the  democrats go to the public and say we  got you this  because remember it's not just an  infrastructure plan folks it is a jobs  plan  that is widely supported by members of  both parties out there in america  so again this is only looking at this  through  nonpartisan eyes trump saying  do not support this that is  what the republicans would be doing  except of course  the other side of that strategy and this  is where trump is totally wrong on it  as i just mentioned majority of  republicans out there support this  heck a majority of republicans even  support raising taxes  on the wealthy and corporations to pay  for it they supported it before it was  even cut down to 1.2 trillion they liked  it when it was three and a half trillion  they want the plan so they would be less  likely in turn  based on that to believe republican  talking points  that democrats were unable to deliver  because they're clearly paying at least  somewhat attention to this issue  and that's another positive development  they know who's holding this thing up  they know that they want it and they  know that republicans and to a degree  mansion and cinema don't want them to  have it  so that's why republicans are stuck  between the rock and a hard place here  on terms of strategy  they want to get democrats to lose  but they can't have their voters who  support this bill  know that they were the ones who kept it  from making it to them  so i think at this point some of them  clearly not all of them but i do think  some of them  have looked at this and said you know  what the best path forward for us  is probably to let this thing happen  at least hey maybe then if there are  some positive developments out of it  once it passes  i can go back to my constituents and  tell them i supported this thing i did  this for you  i did this for you so that could likely  be the strategy that these people take  moving forward and  of course there's also the third part  and that is who cares if trump withholds  his endorsement  there was a study that came out last  week and i actually uh  spoke about this on my other channels  because it's a phenomenal study i love  it  they looked at races where donald trump  endorsed a candidate  versus races where donald trump did not  endorse a candidate  and the political scientists who looked  at all of these endorsements and  all of the outcomes came to a  statistical conclusion  that a donald trump endorsement  makes you two and a half percent less  likely to win your race  candidates who received the trump  endorsement again  two and a half percent not two and a  half times two and a half percent  less likely to win so it's a very very  tiny tiny  disadvantage but it's a disadvantage  nonetheless  and the report also did mention that  yeah when trump endorses a candidate  they end up raising a ton more money but  you know who else does  their opponent every time trump comes  out and endorses somebody they raise  more money  but so does their opponent they also  found that  voter turnout actually does increase in  races where donald trump endorses a  candidate  but again in most instances it benefits  the opponent  not the person trump endorsed so trump  wants to be the king maker he's out  there pretending to be the king maker  he's threatening them  trying to scare them into submission  saying i'm not going to endorse you if  you don't do this and republicans need  to respond with  respond with uh good like please don't  endorse me in fact could you endorse my  primary opponent  because i really want to win this  election  and your endorsement at this point is  effectively a kiss of death  you're not helping candidates you're  hurting them you're  literally making things more difficult  for  them so don't come out there acting like  i'm gonna withhold my endorsement don't  threaten us with a good time man  we've seen the numbers we know what the  data looks like we know that your  endorsement  doesn't change people's minds  and when it does it changes them in  favor of the other  candidate so again republicans you're  not  actually stuck between the rock and the  hard place here  you've got a pretty easy out vote in  favor of the infrastructure package go  back to your constituents tell them that  you delivered it for them  and give donald donald trump the finger  on the way out the door  because trust me you don't want his  endorsement  unless of course you're looking forward  to early retirement that would really be  the only  thing that would work in your favor at  that point
 

